Check each value’s complement before storing its index, so the two indices are always distinct. Expected time: O(n); space: O(n).

```javascript
function solve(nums, target) {
  const seen = new Map();
  for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
    const complement = target - nums[i];
    if (seen.has(complement)) {
      return [seen.get(complement), i];
    }
    seen.set(nums[i], i);
  }
}
```

Call solve(nums, target) directly; the contract guarantees exactly one valid pair.

